canhrActi raw accelerometer pipeline: third-party notices

canhrActi is copyright (c) 2025 CANHR, University of Alaska Fairbanks, all rights
reserved (see the package LICENSE file). The raw accelerometer pipeline in
canhrActi (the R/raw_*.R files and R/circadian_ggir.R) contains code ported
from the open source package GGIR, the conversion of raw data to counts
(R/gt3x_counts.R) restates steps of the open source package agcounts, and the
pipeline calls three further open source packages at run time. This file
records what was taken from where, under which licence, and what is owed in
return.

canhrActi is not GGIR. It is not endorsed by, affiliated with, or supported by
the GGIR authors, the Medical Research Council UK, Accelting, or the French
National Research Agency. The name GGIR is used in this package only to
identify the origin of ported code and to describe which GGIR functions a
canhrActi function reproduces. Nothing in canhrActi should be described or
branded as GGIR, and questions about canhrActi's behaviour should go to the
canhrActi maintainer, not to the GGIR project.

