GGIR ships no NOTICE file, so there is no NOTICE text to reproduce here.

The following canhrActi files contain code ported from GGIR R/ sources, from
3.3-9 unless marked (3.3-6). Each is a MODIFIED version of the original; each
begins with a header that names the GGIR file it was ported from and
summarises what was changed.

Reading, calibration, non-wear and day summaries (GGIR parts 1 and 2):

    R/raw_params.R                 GGIR R/load_params.R, check_params.R
    R/raw_inspect.R                GGIR R/g.inspectfile.R, inspect_binFile_brand.R, g.dotorcomma.R,
                                   g.extractheadervars.R, extractID.R, get_nw_clip_block_params.R
    R/raw_read_block.R             GGIR R/g.readaccfile.R, updateBlocksize.R
    R/raw_impute_timegaps.R        GGIR R/g.imputeTimegaps.R
    R/raw_calibrate.R              GGIR R/g.calibrate.R
    R/raw_metrics.R                GGIR R/g.applymetrics.R and the metric helper files it calls
    R/raw_nonwear.R                GGIR R/detect_nonwear_clipping.R
    R/raw_starttime.R              GGIR R/g.getstarttime.R, get_starttime_weekday_truncdata.R
    R/raw_getmeta.R                GGIR R/g.getmeta.R
    R/raw_weardec.R                GGIR R/g.weardec.R
    R/raw_impute.R                 GGIR R/g.impute.R, g.analyse.R
    R/raw_analyse_perday.R         GGIR R/g.analyse.perday.R (3.3-6)
    R/raw_analyse_perfile.R        GGIR R/g.analyse.perfile.R, g.analyse.R (3.3-6)
    R/raw_getmx.R                  GGIR R/g.getM5L5.R (3.3-6)
    R/raw_quality.R                GGIR R/g.part1.R, g.part2.R, g.analyse.perday.R, g.impute.R
                                   (the validity checks behind data_quality_report.csv)
    R/raw_pipeline.R               GGIR R/g.part1.R
    R/raw_constants.R              GGIR R/monitor_types.R

Sleep (GGIR parts 3 and 4):

    R/raw_sleep_detect.R           GGIR R/g.sib.det.R
    R/raw_sleep_sib.R              GGIR R/HASIB.R
    R/raw_sleep_guider.R           GGIR R/HASPT.R
    R/raw_sleep_guider_correct.R   GGIR R/g.part3_correct_guider.R, g.part3_alignIndexVectors.R
    R/raw_sleep_summary.R          GGIR R/g.sib.sum.R
    R/raw_sleep_part3.R            GGIR R/g.part3.R
    R/raw_sleep_nights.R           GGIR R/g.part4.R, g.create.sp.mat.R, is_this_a_dst_night.R
    R/raw_sleep_sri.R              GGIR R/CalcSleepRegularityIndex.R
    R/raw_sleeplog.R               GGIR R/g.loadlog.R, g.part4_extractid.R
    R/raw_sleep_report.R           GGIR R/g.report.part4.R, tidyup_df.R, addSplitNames.R,
                                   getSplitNames.R

Time use (GGIR part 5):

    R/raw_timeuse.R                GGIR R/g.part5.R
    R/raw_timeuse_windows.R        GGIR R/g.part5.definedays.R, g.part5.wakesleepwindows.R and
                                   the midnight and night-trimming blocks of g.part5.R
    R/raw_timeuse_series.R         GGIR R/g.part5_initialise_ts.R, g.part5.addsib.R,
                                   g.part5.handle_lux_extremes.R, is.ISO8601.R
    R/raw_timeuse_segment.R        GGIR R/g.part5_analyseSegment.R, g.part5.lux_persegment.R
    R/raw_timeuse_levels.R         GGIR R/g.getbout.R, identify_level.R
    R/raw_timeuse_fragmentation.R  GGIR R/g.fragmentation.R, g.intensitygradient.R
    R/raw_timeuse_rest.R           GGIR R/g.part5.analyseRest.R, markerButtonForRest.R
    R/raw_timeuse_sibreport.R      GGIR R/g.sibreport.R
    R/raw_timeuse_timeseries.R     GGIR R/g.part5.savetimeseries.R
    R/raw_timeuse_report.R         GGIR R/g.report.part5.R
    R/raw_timeuse_dictionary.R     GGIR R/g.report.part5_dictionary.R,
                                   dev-functions/createInternalData.R

Exports, figures and circadian:

    R/raw_export.R                 GGIR R/g.part1.R to g.part5.R, g.part5.savetimeseries.R,
                                   g.report.part5.R, g.report.part5_dictionary.R,
                                   checkMilestoneFolders.R, correctOlderMilestoneData.R
    R/raw_plots.R                  GGIR R/g.plot.R, visualReport.R, g.sib.plot.R, g.plot5.R
    R/raw_sleep_plots.R            GGIR R/g.sib.plot.R and the visualisation_sleep block of
                                   g.part4.R
    R/raw_timeuse_plots.R          GGIR R/visualReport.R (the part-5 class ribbon),
                                   g.intensitygradient.R
    R/raw_ggir_panelplot.R         GGIR R/visualReport.R, blocks copied verbatim (3.3-6)
    R/raw_ggir_sleepplot.R         GGIR R/g.part4.R, the drawing calls copied (3.3-6)
    R/circadian_ggir.R             GGIR R/cosinor_IS_IV_Analyses.R, g.IVIS.R, blocks copied
                                   verbatim (3.3-6)

The header at the top of each of these files is the authoritative statement
of which GGIR source it was ported from; the list above is a summary.

Modifications, in general terms: file input and output, console printing and
GGIR's params object were removed or replaced with explicit arguments and
return values; functions and files were renamed to canhrActi conventions;
a small number of canhrActi-only behaviours were added behind parameters that
default to GGIR's behaviour. The arithmetic of the ported code was kept as it
is in GGIR so that results are reproducible against GGIR output.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. GGIRread (called only, no code copied)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Package:     GGIRread, Wearable Accelerometer Data File Readers
Version:     1.0.8 as installed and tested; 1.0.10 as read in source
Repository:  https://github.com/wadpac/GGIRread/
Licence:     Apache License, Version 2.0 (the same text as inst/LICENSE.GGIR)

Copyright holders: Medical Research Council UK (cph, fnd); Accelting (cph, fnd).

Authors and contributors (Authors@R, version 1.0.10):
    Vincent T van Hees (aut, cre)
    Patrick Bos (aut)
    Lena Kushleyeva (ctb)
    Jing Hua Zhao (ctb)
    Evgeny Mirkes (ctb)
    Dan Jackson (ctb)
    Jairo H Migueles (ctb)
    John Muschelli (ctb)

The Axivity .cwa reading code in GGIRread (AxivityNumUnpack, readAxivity) was
originally written by Evgeny Mirkes (University of Leicester) and revised by
Dan Jackson, as credited in the GGIRread source files.

canhrActi uses GGIRread by calling its exported functions (readGENEActiv,
readAxivity, readParmayMatrix, resample) through the installed package. No
GGIRread R or C++ source has been copied into canhrActi.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. read.gt3x (called only, no code copied)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Package:     read.gt3x, Parse ActiGraph GT3X/GT3X+ Accelerometer Data
Version:     1.2.0 as installed and tested; 1.3.0 as read in source
Repository:  https://github.com/THLfi/read.gt3x
Licence:     European Union Public Licence (EUPL), version 1.1 or 1.2
             (declared as "EUPL" in the package DESCRIPTION)

Authors: Tuomo Nieminen (aut, cre), John Muschelli (aut);
contributors Patrick Bos (ctb), Vincent van Hees (ctb).

canhrActi uses read.gt3x by calling its exported functions (read.gt3x,
parse_gt3x_info and related helpers) through the installed package. No
read.gt3x R or C++ source has been copied into canhrActi. The EUPL is a
copyleft licence, and canhrActi deliberately does not derive from read.gt3x
code. The .gt3x reader in src/gt3x_stream.cpp was written from ActiGraph's
published format description (https://github.com/actigraph/GT3X-File-Format)
and only checked against read.gt3x output; it contains no read.gt3x code.

